# Django Templates

- Pages extend `base.html`. HTMX fragments use `_partial.html` names.
- `{% url %}` instead of hardcoded paths. `{% empty %}` on loops that can be empty.
- Keep logic out of templates; use model methods (`user.can_moderate`).
- POST forms include `{% csrf_token %}`, render fields through
  `components/_field.html`, and show `partials/_form_errors.html`.
- `500.html` stays standalone: no context processors, no `user`, no database.
- Wrap user-visible copy in `{% translate %}` / `{% blocktranslate %}`.

See skills: `django-templates`, `htmx-patterns`.
